1. what is angular js and its benefit?
Ans: angularJS is a structural javascript framework that help to build dynamic SPAs using
features like two-way data binding, MVC architecture, and dependency injection.
it was developed by google and helps developers write cleaner , organized frontend code.
main benefits
1. two-way data binding:
when data changes in the UI- it update the model.
when model changes - Ui updates automatically.
less manual DOM work.
2. MVC structure
separates:
model - data
view - UI
controller - logic
⟶ code becomes clean and easy to manage.
3. dependency injection
automatically provides required services/components.
easier testing & modular code.
4. directives
you can create custom HTML tags and behaviors.
reusable ui components
5. templates
HTML + dynamic data = fast page updates
6. routing
used to switch view wihtout reloading the page.
7. testing friendly
designed to support unit testing and end-to-end testing.
2. Mvc architecture in angularJS
Ans:
MVC = model + view + controller
it is a way to organize code so it becomes clean and easy to manage.
1) Model
contains data of the application
example:
username
product list
price
it is the business information
2) view
what the user sees , it talk about UI of the application
HTML page
example:
buttons
form
tables
3) Controller
-connect model and view
-handles logic and user actions
example:
get data
update data
respond to click events
how they work together
controller sends data – view
user changes something in view
model updates
updated data shows automatically in view
example:
Model ⟶ name = “sachin”
view ⟶ show sachin
if value becomes “rahul” ⟶ screen updates automatically
3. ng-app, ng-click ng-init, ng-hide and show, ng-model, ng-repeat, binding expalin with code
and detail
ans:
a) ng-app
starts the angularJS application
it tells where angular should work
<html ng-app>
without this ⟶ angular will not run
b) ng-init
used to initialize(start) data
<div ng-init=”name=’Sachin’”>
{{name}}
</div>
output ⟶ sachin
c) data binding {{ }}
shows data from model to UI.
<div ng-init=”city=’mUMBAI’ ”>
{{ city }}
</div>
if value change ⟶ Ui update automatically
d) ng-model
connect input box with data
<input type="text" ng-model="username">
<p>Hello {{username}}</p>
e) ng-click
runs function when button is clicked
<button ng-click="count = count + 1">Click</button>
<p>{{count}}</p>
f) ng-show & ng-hide
show or hide elements based on condition
ng-show example
<button ng-click="visible=true">Show</button>
<p ng-show="visible">Hello</p>\
ng-hide example
<button ng-click="hidden=true">Hide</button>
<p ng-hide="hidden">Bye</p>
g) ng-repeat
used for looping (array, lists)
<div ng-init="fruits=['Apple', 'Mango'
, 'Banana']">
<ul>
<li ng-repeat="f in fruits">{{f}}</li>
</ul>
</div>
ouput:
apple
mango
banana
4. angular js filter & their types
Ans:
Filters are used to format or modify data before showing it in the UI.
- the data is same , just display style changes
syntax:
{{ data | filterName }}
common filter types are:
1) upper case
convert text ⟶ capital
ouput ⟶ sachin
2) lowercase
convert text ⟶ small letters
{{ "SACHIN" | lowercase }}
output---> sachin
3) currency
format number as money
{{ 500 | currency }}
4) date
formal date
{{ today | date:'dd/MM/yyyy' }}
5) number
control decimal places
example:
{{ 1234.567 | number:2 }}
output ⟶ 1234.57
6) limit to
limits characters or items
{{ "AngularJS" | limitTo:7 }}
output ⟶ angular
7) filter
search / find in list.
<input ng-model="search">
<li ng-repeat="p in products | filter:search">
{{p}}
</li>
Multiple filter together
{{ "sachin" | uppercase | limitTo:4 }}
output ⟶ SACH
5. routing in angularJS for single page applications(SPAs)
ans: routing in AngularJS is a mechanism that allows navigation between different views of an
application without reloading the entire page. Since an SPA loads only one main HTML file,
routing dynamically changes the content based on the URL.
module used:: angularJS provides routing using the ngRoute module
how routing work
when the URL changes, angularJS:
1. Matches it with a defined route.
2. loads the required template.
3. attaches the specified controller.
4. display the view inside the <ng-show> directive .
advantages:
no full page reload
faster navigation
better user experience
easy management of multiple views
6. validation in angular js : normal validation and custom validation
ans: Validation in AngularJS is used to ensure that the user enters correct and complete data
in forms.
validation rules.
AngularJS provides built-in (normal) validation and also allows us to create custom
a) normal validation
angularJS automatically checks form field using directives.
common validation directives
required - field cannot be empty
ng-minlength - minimum characters
ng-maxlenght - maximum characters
type=”email” - valid email format
type = “number” - only numbers
b) custom validation
when built-in rules are not enough, we create our own validation logic using directives
example situation
password length
confirm password
age limit
special format
7. sorting data and search filter in angularJS
ans: In AngularJS, sorting and filtering are mainly done using filters inside ng-repeat.
They help display data in a user-friendly way without changing the original data.
a) sorting data (orderBy filter)
angularJS provide the orderBy filter to arrange items in ascending or descending order
syntax:
ng-repeat=”Item in items | orderBy: ‘fieldName’”
b) search filter
the filter is used to search specific data from a list based on user input.
syntax
ng-repeat=”item in items | filter:searchText”
combine sorting + searching
<li ng-repeat”emp in employees | filter;searchText | orderBy:’’name”>
{{ emp.name }}
</li>